{
  "$comment": [
    "Which ETP message answers which: not in the .avsc schemas, so declared here,",
    "and held against the schemas by `request_response_table_is_honest`",
    "(crates/retp-tests/tests/correlation.rs). doc/design/etp-et-osdu/client-etp.md \u00a74 bis.",
    "Source: ETP Specification v1.2 / Document v1.1, the \"Correlation Id Usage\" line",
    "of every message section; `section` is where. Keys are `Namespace.Message`,",
    "because four names repeat across protocols (ChannelData, Chunk, ...).",
    "Guessing \"X answers X + Response\" would hold 120 times and fail on the first",
    "message of every conversation: RequestSession is answered by OpenSession.",
    "- responses: each response and the request(s) it is correlated to;",
    "- alsoNotification: responses that may also be sent unprompted, with a zero",
    "  correlationId (\"When sent as a notification\");",
    "- chunks: a Chunk travels inside a multipart message and shares its correlation;",
    "- universal: may answer any message (\u00a73.7.2);",
    "- privateProtocols: numbers 2000 and up, which the specification does not cover;",
    "- errata: where the specification names a message that does not exist.",
    "Every other message is uncorrelated: a request if some response names it,",
    "one-way otherwise. That is derived, not declared."
  ],
